ore release.", "reviewers": ["code-owner"], "idempotency_key": "money-half-even-pr-08d3cd5986", "confidence": 0.85}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The PR is open as #101. Merging into main requires code-owner approval under policy, so I'll submit the merge request and check whether it's held for approval.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01S84gGq1AYwT8bpRn7sBMjZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"number": 101, "confidence": 0.7}, "name": "merge_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The nightly failure is fixed and the change is merged into main as PR #101 (merge commit `08d3cd5986`).\n\n- **Root cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but FIN-212 and `tests/test_money.py` require `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n- **Fix:** I changed the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on branch `fix/money-half-even-rounding`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` on that commit passed.\n- **PR:** Opened #101 against main, with `code-owner` as reviewer.\n- **Merge:** The merge went through with a recorded human approval (\"Approved. Looks right.\"), so the policy requirement was met.\n\nI did not verify that the change is included in today's release build. Rounding now differs for exact half-cent values (e.g. 2.675 \u2192 2.68, 2.665 \u2192 2.66), so downstream consumers may see different results.", "type": "text"}]}]}